- memory bloc 1453075200: no/value
+ memory bloc 1453075200: Death Is Not The EndValue: Editorial Promotion Seeds New Life
+ My first news of No Man’s Sky was thanks to a short feature from one of my favorite science fiction authors, relaying how he played the game for hours with the hilarious sole purpose of provoking in-game death so he could see which of his quotations the developers had included as a “Game Over” notification. From this short piece, the concept of No Man’s Sky leapt out at me; “video games” typically don’t catch my interest, but this was different. NMS called to me on a new frequency. It was some time (and a computer acquisition) later before I could begin my own journey, but I knew then that my first steps were inevitable, eventual, and would constitute a new beginning, a dream I could share with others, among the stars …
+ Memory compliance: 100%
